#8 143.2 Your choice: [1]> TERM environment variable not set.
#8 143.2 This script will do a few things to make sure the script can be run
#8 143.2 without too much fuss. First it will check to see if all binaries are
#8 143.2 present. If binaries are missing in /glftpd/bin, it will try to copy
#8 143.2 the needed ones there. All binaries listed will be chmod'ed ugoa+rx.
#8 143.2 Should a binary fail to be found, this program will exit, and you must
#8 143.2 either broaden the path or copy the file yourself. If the script cannot
#8 143.2 chmod the binaries, it will NOT exit, but it will report it, leaving
#8 143.2 you to make sure it has the correct permissions.
#8 143.2 
#8 143.2 It will then check all needed logfiles, creating those not present and
#8 143.2 chmod them ugoa-rw. Should this fail, this program will abort, leaving
#8 143.2 you to fix it.
#8 143.2 Lastly, it will check to see if your config-file is world readable.
#8 143.2 
#8 143.2 It will not currently check permissions on psxc-imdb.sh or the tcl-files
#8 143.2 if you use them, so you're on your own there. And this is no substitute
#8 143.2 for a brain... Things could still go wrong.
#8 143.2 
#8 143.2 PRESS <RETURN> TO CONTINUE
#8 143.2 TERM environment variable not set.
#8 143.2 This script will not do Something Bad to your files, and should be quite
#8 143.2 safe to run whenever you wish/need to. Please remember this if a future
#8 143.2 upgrade leaves you hanging high and dry - running this script might be
#8 143.2 able to fix your problem. If new files are introduced, this script will be
#8 143.2 updated, so make sure you use the most recent one availible.
#8 143.2 
#8 143.2 New in this version is the ability to check dependencies of the binaries
#8 143.2 in /glftpd/bin - the ones we need in any case.
#8 143.2 If you wish to run it, write 'depcheck'. It will first remove all the
#8 143.2 needed binaries in /glftpd/bin, then copy them back from your environment
#8 143.2 as well as copy any missing libs the binaries need.
#8 143.2 If you are nervous, you should make a backup of /glftpd/bin before
#8 143.2 doing this, or use psxc-depcheck.sh after copying the bins.
#8 143.2 
#8 143.2 Press <RETURN> or 'depcheck' to Start, <CTRL-C> to Break
